Response-side checks: CNAME targets and answer addresses are checked
against the allow lists first and then the deny lists.

-- list ads block adblock --
||tracker.example^
@@||ok.tracker.example^
192.0.2.66
@@198.51.100.1
||198.51.100.1^
-- list fix allow domains --
allowed-cname.example
-- list other block hosts --
0.0.0.0 allowed-cname.example
-- counts ads --
rules=5 exceptions=2 entries=5
-- expect --
cname:cdn.tracker.example     block ads ||tracker.example^
cname:CDN.Tracker.Example.    block ads ||tracker.example^
cname:ok.tracker.example      pass    # in-list exception
cname:allowed-cname.example   pass    # allow lists apply to answers too
cname:clean.example           pass
ip:192.0.2.66                 block ads 192.0.2.66
ip:::ffff:192.0.2.66          block ads 192.0.2.66
ip:192.0.2.67                 pass
ip:198.51.100.1               pass    # in-list IP exception
tracker.example               block ads ||tracker.example^
